Stack: Project Selection

Purpose:
  Project-specific technology stack selections. These files are selected
  instances from the root .sdd/stack/ technology catalog. Each selection
  is documented with rationale and alternative choices.

  Stack templates live at @../../../templates/_sdd/stack/.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1  @INDEX.sdd (this file — project stack map)
   2  @LAYER.template.sdd (stack layer template)
   3  @<layer>.sdd (specific layer selection, when populated)

Modes:
  ANALYZE   — stack fit and compatibility analysis
  PLAN      — technology selection and mapping
  WORK      — stack-based implementation
  VERIFY    — stack compliance check
  REVIEW    — technology decision execution

Rules:
  [PS1]  Project stack MUST be selected from root .sdd/stack/ catalog.
  [PS2]  Technology selection MUST be recorded with rationale.
  [PS3]  Stack compatibility (all layers) MUST be validated.
  [PS4]  Version policy MUST follow root stack/ guidelines.
  [PS5]  Technology changes require TECH_UPDATE_PROPOSAL.
  [PS6]  Cross-layer impact MUST be analyzed on stack changes.

Entry:
  Read:
    INDEX.sdd

  Resolve:
    backend
    frontend
    mobile
    database
    testing
    infrastructure

Navigation:
  ProjectStack: @projects/sddra.ai/stack/INDEX.sdd
  Backend: @projects/sddra.ai/stack/backend.sdd
  Frontend: @projects/sddra.ai/stack/frontend.sdd
  Mobile: @projects/sddra.ai/stack/mobile.sdd
  Database: @projects/sddra.ai/stack/database.sdd
  Testing: @projects/sddra.ai/stack/testing.sdd
  Infrastructure: @projects/sddra.ai/stack/infrastructure.sdd
  RootStack: @stack/INDEX.sdd
  Template: @../../../templates/_sdd/stack/LAYER.template.sdd

State: +

Note:
  This file is the project-specific stack map. It points to
  detailed stack files and references the root stack knowledge base.
  Concrete stack selections are generated per project by the
  project-structure skill from templates/_sdd/stack/.
